<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 130,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 130,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it bought 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 50,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Australian barley and 20,000 tonnes of U.S. barley in its weekly tender.</p>
<p>The purchases, excluding the 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat for July shipment, are for August shipment.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p> WHEAT</p>
<p> COUNTRY    QUANTITY</p>
<p> U.S.	 60,000    Dark Northern Spring  30,000</p>
<p>			    Hard Red Winter</p>
<p>			    (Protein 13.0 pct)    20,000</p>
<p>			    (Protein 11.5 pct)    10,000</p>
<p> Canada     50,000    1CW			 34,000</p>
<p>			    Durum		     16,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000    Prime hard		20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Australia  20,000    Feed			20,000</p>
<p> U.S.	 20,000    Feed			20,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
